>
> I don't see how either of those could mean "always and everywhere: the
> whole of time and space"
>

Also, keep in mind that I'm specifically talking about, for example: {roroi
fe'eroroi pa da zo'u da prenu} : "In the whole of time and space there is
exactly one X, such that X is a person.", which is what {pa prenu} means if
you /don't/ limit it to context. (If you do limit it to context, {pa prenu}
means pretty much the same thing {pa lo prenu} does, as latro'a pointed
out.)


